      },
      "children": []
    },
    "sd-loop": {
      "id": "sd-loop",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The main flow is initial Sync and backfill, Run, an epoch boundary and save point, Sync, and resume. Pausing can also lead into Sync. Workers use the game's knowledge and return attempt records. Librarian processing turns supported findings into cited facts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "sd-state": {
      "id": "sd-state",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Harness State is the durable record of progress. Dispatch State controls leases and permission to execute work. The harness connects those responsibilities to the game checkout and knowledge base."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
